* CABSRT17 - INVOICE HEADER SORT FOR THE CLOSE
* MVT OS/360 SORT/MERGE FORM OF JCL/CTLCARDS/CABSRT17.
* SORTS THE FINAL INVOICE HEADERS BY LEDGER COMPANY AND BILL
* PERIOD FOR THE MONTH END CLOSE.  THE LEDGER COMPANY IS NOT A
* FIELD ON THE HEADER - IT IS DERIVED FROM THE FIRST TWO BYTES
* OF THE INVOICE NUMBER, WHICH IS THE PREFIX CABBIL12 PUT THERE.
*
* THE RULES THAT LEFT THIS CARD
*   THE INREC OPERAND THAT MOVED THAT PREFIX TO THE FRONT OF THE
*   RECORD IS NOT CODED HERE, AND NEITHER IS THE OUTREC OPERAND
*   THAT PUT IT BACK.  THIS SORT HAS NO INREC AND NO OUTREC
*   STATEMENT.
*   THE E15 EXIT CABSXLDG NOW TAKES BYTES 24 AND 25 AND PUTS
*   THEM IN FRONT OF THE 400 BYTE HEADER, PRODUCING A 402 BYTE
*   RECORD AND SETTING THE LENGTH WORD IN THE E15 PARAMETER LIST
*   TO 402.
*   THE E35 EXIT CABSXLDR TAKES THOSE TWO BYTES BACK OFF ON THE
*   WAY OUT AND SETS THE LENGTH WORD TO 400, SO THE CLOSE
*   PROGRAM READS THE ORIGINAL LAYOUT IT HAS ALWAYS READ.
*
* THE KEY POSITIONS BELOW ARE THE POSITIONS IN THE RESHAPED
* RECORD, BECAUSE CABSXLDG RESHAPES IT BEFORE THE SORT SEES IT.
* 1,2 IS THE LEDGER COMPANY PREFIX AND 17,6 IS THE BILL PERIOD,
* WHICH SITS AT 15 ON THE FILE THE CLOSE PROGRAM READS.
*
* OPTION EQUALS IS NOT CODED - THIS SORT HAS NO OPTION
* STATEMENT.  THE CLOSE TAKES A TOTAL PER LEDGER COMPANY AND
* PERIOD AND DOES NOT DEPEND ON THE ORDER WITHIN ONE.
*
* WHERE THE LEDGER COMPANY COMES FROM IS NO LONGER READABLE FROM
* THIS CONTROL CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(1,2,CH,A,17,6,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=(402)
 MODS E15=(CABSXLDG,4096,SORTEXIT,N),E35=(CABSXLDR,4096,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
